      "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\n\n    // Each key sorts first by diagonal, then by row.\n    vector<unsigned long long> blockedCells;\n    blockedCells.reserve(static_cast<size_t>(m));\n    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\n        int row, column;\n        cin >> row >> column;\n        unsigned long long diagonal = static_cast<unsigned long long>(row + column);\n        blockedCells.push_back(diagonal * static_cast<unsigned long long>(n) +\n                               static_cast<unsigned long long>(row));\n    }\n    sort(blockedCells.begin(), blockedCells.end());\n\n    vector<int> previous(n, 0);\n    vector<int> current(n, 0);\n    vector<int> blockedStamp(n, -1);\n    size_t blockedIndex = 0;\n\n    while (blockedIndex < blockedCells.size() &&\n           blockedCells[blockedIndex] / static_cast<unsigned long long>(n) == 0) {\n        blockedStamp[static_cast<size_t>(blockedCells[blockedIndex] %\n                                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(n))] = 0;\n        ++blockedIndex;\n    }\n    previous[0] = blockedStamp[0] == 0 ? 0 : 1;\n\n    for (int diagonal = 1; diagonal <= 2 * n - 2; ++diagonal) {\n        const bool growing = diagonal < n;\n        const int lowRow = growing ? 0 : diagonal - n + 1;\n        const int length = growing ? diagonal + 1 : 2 * n - 1 - diagonal;\n\n        while (blockedIndex < blockedCells.size() &&\n               blockedCells[blockedIndex] / static_cast<unsigned long long>(n) ==\n                   static_cast<unsigned long long>(diagonal)) {\n            const int row = static_cast<int>(blockedCells[blockedIndex] %\n                                             static_cast<unsigned long long>(n));\n            blockedStamp[row - lowRow] = diagonal;\n            ++blockedIndex;\n        }\n\n        const int* __restrict__ previousData = previous.data();\n        int* __restrict__ currentData = current.data();\n        const int* __restrict__ stampData = blockedStamp.data();\n\n        if (growing) {\n            const int last = length - 1;\n            currentData[0] = stampData[0] == diagonal ? 0 : previousData[0];\n            currentData[last] = stampData[last] == diagonal ? 0 : previousData[last - 1];\n\n            #pragma GCC ivdep\n            for (int i = 1; i < last; ++i) {\n                int ways = previousData[i - 1] + previousData[i];\n                if (ways >= MOD) ways -= MOD;\n                currentData[i] = stampData[i] == diagonal ? 0 : ways;\n            }\n        } else {\n            #pragma GCC ivdep\n            for (int i = 0; i < length; ++i) {\n                int ways = previousData[i] + previousData[i + 1];\n                if (ways >= MOD) ways -= MOD;\n                currentData[i] = stampData[i] == diagonal ? 0 : ways;\n            }\n        }\n\n        previous.swap(current);\n    }\n\n    cout << previous[0] << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Sweeping the grid by anti-diagonals makes cells within each wavefront independent: each reads only the preceding wavefront, so GCC can legally SIMD-vectorize the contiguous inner loops. Rolling wavefront buffers also remove the baseline's full blocked matrix and per-row copy.",
  "notes": "The recurrence retains dependencies between successive diagonals; only independent cells within a diagonal are marked ivdep. Blocked cells are sorted and tracked with O(N) stamps, preserving the input's (row, column) interpretation and blocked-start/end behavior. No documentation was requested.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Reordered the dynamic program into anti-diagonal wavefronts and used two rolling O(N) buffers, swapping rather than copying rows.",
    "Replaced the N×N blocked bitmap with sorted diagonal/row keys and O(N) timestamp storage.",
    "Marked dependency-free inner wavefront loops for GCC SIMD and replaced modulo operations on two reduced values with one conditional subtraction."
